WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.690
I’m going start this episode with a question.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:11.930
And please, don’t cheat…

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.600
don’t google the answer.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.109
What is the country with the biggest share
of female politicians inside of its parliament?

00:00:18.109 --> 00:00:21.779
You might be thinking of Norway, Sweden or…
perhaps Great Britain, right?

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:24.490
If that is the case… you are thinking wrong.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:29.310
The answer is actually RWANDA, one of the
poorest places in sub Saharan Africa.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:33.880
I’m sure many of you already know this country.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.170
At least, those of you who are as old as me...

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:42.680
In the year 1994, the Rwandan genocide appeared
on every news station around the World.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.230
It was one of the biggest atrocities of mankind
in history.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:50.910
In just 100 days, the Rwandan government brutally
killed almost one million people…

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:54.130
. This meant that 1 out of every 5 Rwandans
was murdered.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:01:00.050
For decades, Rwanda was a synonym for humanitarian
catastrophe, starvation and a memory of the

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.610
darkest side of the human condition.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:09.580
Nonetheless, 23 years later in the year 2017,
Rwanda is turning into something much different...

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.909
“Reflections from Rwanda: investing in one
of the World’s fastest-growing economies”

00:01:14.909 --> 00:01:16.730
Yep, you heard that right.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:20.040
Rwanda is becoming a hot topic in the financial
world.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:25.450
A country that used to appear on humaniarian
aid commercials, now is starting to fill financial

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:26.450
newspapers.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.940
And its president, Paul Kagame, has become
the new African rock star, being received

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:34.229
at prestigious places like Harvard or the
Brookings Institution.

00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:38.630
Yes, of course, everyone agrees that his style
is kind of authoritarian.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:43.400
Winning elections with over 96% of the vote
doesn’t sound quite democratic, does it?

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.740
But, despite all of that, who can judge the
man who is taking Rwanda out of poverty?

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.460
The figures speak for themselves.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:53.250
Since Paul Kagame came into power, Rwandans
have tripled their income, and the percentage

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:58.049
of the population that lives in extreme poverty
is reducing year after year.

00:01:58.049 --> 00:02:01.990
So now the question is…

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.900
How did Rwanda end up like this?

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.650
Or perhaps: is this too good to be true?

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.729
Is there some detail we are missing here?

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:13.861
Today we are going to answer these questions
but before we do, let’s take a look back

00:02:13.861 --> 00:02:15.080
at history.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:21.140
And trust me, this is a pretty intense story…

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.760
PREFABRICATED HATRED

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:26.569
Remember this date: April 6th 1994.

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:31.330
On this date, the plane the Rwandan president
was flying in was hit by an anti-aircraft

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:36.030
gun.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.360
No one really knows who organized this attack.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:43.110
But the Rwandan army, whose soldiers belonged
to the HUTU tribe, blamed their rival tribe:

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.110
THE TUTSIS.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.360
Tutsis were a minority inside of Rwanda living
in an apartheid situation.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.480
Local media referred to them as ´COCKROACHES´
and many of them had already escaped to refugee

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.360
camps in neighbouring countries.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.319
But no one could have predicted that the mounting
prejudice would unleash such carnage.

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:10.690
´This is a warning message to all those cockroaches
listening to us…

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:18.980
Rwanda belongs to those who really defend
it.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:25.030
Tutsis are not even 8% of the population.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:35.880
If we exterminate them, no one will judge
us because we will win”

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:40.060
While messages like this were broadcasted
on the radio, the Rwandan army was passing

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:42.500
out clubs and machetes to civilians.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:46.959
If any of those HUTU civilians showed mercy
to his or her TUTSI neighbours, he or she

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:52.230
would risk being executed as a collaborator…

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:58.160
This explains why many Rwandans clubbed their
tutsi wives to death and why even some Catholic

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.680
churches became human slaughterhouses.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:08.379
In just 100 days, almost 1 million people
died by their neighbours machetes.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:09.819
And now you might wonder…

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:12.019
Why did the HUTUS hate the TUTSIS so much?

00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:14.209
Were they really that different?

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:19.389
The answer is NO.

00:04:19.389 --> 00:04:30.690
You see, many African countries have lots
of different cultures and races living together.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.910
South Africa, for example, has 9 official
languages.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:38.900
Uganda has over 15.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:44.120
Nonetheless, Rwandan territory was surprisingly
homogenous for centuries.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:45.280
One single language.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.370
One single culture.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:50.060
The hutus, the tutsis, and other tribes lived
in relative harmony.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.770
But, in the 20th century, Belgium colonized
this country.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:57.590
One of the first policies made by the Belgian
Government was to force the locals to label

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:01.160
themselves according to the tribe they belonged
to.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:07.880
This way, it would be easier for the colonizers
to identify who was who.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:11.830
And during the first years, the TUTSIS where
the tribe in charge of government institutions

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.180
created by the Belgians.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.090
But one day, those tutsis started asking for
independence.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:20.350
And that’s when Belgium started supporting
the hutus with racist propaganda.

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:25.250
This is how, when Rwanda became a sovereign
state in 1962, Hutus and Tutsis had already

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.650
become fierce enemies.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:29.790
That hatred was fabricated by the colonizers.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:34.760
And many tutsis had to flee to refugee camps
in neighbouring countries.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:42.070
Among them was the man you see on the screen:
PAUL KAGAME.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:45.199
Remember his name because he will be the key
figure in this story.

00:05:45.199 --> 00:05:51.240
Paul Kagame was raised on one of those aforementioned
refugee camps, this one situated in UGANDA.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.150
It was the beginning of the 1980s.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:55.759
Back then, Uganda was in the middle of a civil
war.

00:05:55.759 --> 00:06:05.230
And Kagame, alongside other Rwandan refugees,
fought the Ugandan Government… and won.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.320
This is how Kagame, as a military legend,
was born.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:12.820
In the 90s, he would lead other attacks against
the Hutu-led Rwandan Government.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:20.340
But the turning point was in 1994, 100 days
after that horrific massacre on April the

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.180
6th.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:29.180
Kagame was making his entrance in Kigali,
the Rwandan capital, with 2500 soldiers.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:32.600
The genocide was over and Rwanda had a new
government.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:36.889
This time it was a tutsi-led government with
Kagame serving as the vice president…

00:06:36.889 --> 00:06:40.600
But hold on just a second because the story
doesn’t just end here.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.600
Imagine the scenario…

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:46.410
For one, he had to help lead a divided country,
where the genocide survivors had to live next

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:50.850
to the neighbours that had killed their family
and friends.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:56.810
And it didn’t help that Rwanda was one of
the 10 poorest countries on Earth, with few

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:57.990
resources to export.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:03.090
And on the top of all that, this brand new
Tutsi Government was not an example of transparency

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.100
and respect for Human Rights.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:09.830
As you can imagine, many of the soldiers who
had taken over Kigali wanted revenge.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:15.030
And during the next year, no one made an effort
to stop the executions and the unfair trials.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:18.770
If this wasn’t enough, many ministers tried
to use their positions to fill their pockets

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.820
with the little money Rwanda had.

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:22.650
Corruption was on the rise.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:27.229
Meanwhile, Paul Kagame had the charisma, the
popular support and, especially, the political

00:07:27.229 --> 00:07:29.580
ambition to rise even higher.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:32.690
This is why, in March 2000, the Hutu President
Pasteur Bizimungu resigned.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:36.610
And without an election, well, the inevitable
happened…

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:41.800
KAGAME, THE ETERNAL PRESIDENT

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:45.389
In the year 2000, Paul Kagame became the new
Rwandan president.

00:07:45.389 --> 00:07:48.330
And he came to power with two clear goals.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:52.200
The first one was to unify the Rwandan people
after the genocide.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.380
The second was to pull his country out of
poverty.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:57.380
And what did he do to achieve this latter
goal?

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:59.690
Well, he traveled.

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:02.509
A lot.

00:08:02.509 --> 00:08:08.900
Kagame created an advisory team that went
to countries like CHINA, THAILAND and SINGAPORE.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:11.960
Can you guess what those three places have
in common?

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.050
Oh yes.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:18.330
They were all countries that used to be poor
but, and back then, they were emerging nations.

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:23.650
Kagame arranged meetings with politicians,
economists and civil servants.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:27.319
And from those meetings, he wrote down scores
of ideas in a notebook.

00:08:27.319 --> 00:08:30.880
Then he returned with the golden formula to
build a wealthy country.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:35.860
This notebook became the foundation for the
brand new Rwandan constitution and, more importantly,

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:36.860
Vision 2020.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:41.681
Basically, Vision 2020 was a government development
plan launched by Paul Kagame with the goal

00:08:41.681 --> 00:08:46.769
of transforming Rwanda into a middle income
country in just two decades.

00:08:46.769 --> 00:08:51.079
A modern, peaceful country where extreme poverty
no longer existed.

00:08:51.079 --> 00:08:55.230
But wait a minute because this is not your
typical buzzword-filled politician’s speech!

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:59.540
Rwanda’s Vision 2020 has 44 clear and accountable
goals.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:04.950
For instance, it says that in the year 2020,
1 in every 3 Rwandans must have electricity

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:05.950
at home.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:10.600
And both the Government and private consultancy
firms are analyzing and measuring the progress

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:14.829
on all of those goals.

00:09:14.829 --> 00:09:18.180
So how about an example?

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:19.180
Well here you go:

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:22.389
One of those targets was to make Rwanda a
gender equality haven.

00:09:22.389 --> 00:09:27.649
And now, the Rwandan Constitution requires
that, at least, 50% of all government positions

00:09:27.649 --> 00:09:29.769
be held by women.

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:36.730
In fact, at the time of the making of this
video, the Rwandan parliament has the biggest

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:39.529
share of female MPs in the entire world.

00:09:39.529 --> 00:09:44.100
And the wage gap between men and women is
lower than in countries as progressive as

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.100
Denmark.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:53.839
Today, there is a brand new generation of
female Rwandan entrepreneurs leading the country.

00:09:53.839 --> 00:09:58.239
And what’s more, Rwanda is investing the
little money they collect in taxes pretty

00:09:58.239 --> 00:09:59.239
wisely.

00:09:59.239 --> 00:10:03.310
In a country where 80% of its population used
to live off of subsistence farming, the government

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:08.059
has built power generators and roads that
increase agricultural productivity.

00:10:08.059 --> 00:10:14.100
Now Rwandan farmers are exporting food to
their neighbours.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:20.879
All of this explains why 23 years after the
genocide, Rwanda’s GDP is growing at an

00:10:20.879 --> 00:10:22.970
average rate of 8% a year.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:27.529
&nbsp;This is a similar rate to emerging economies
like China or Vietnam.

00:10:27.529 --> 00:10:31.710
On the same streets where, in 1994, people
where clubbing each other to death, start

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:34.350
ups like the RWANDA MOTORCYCLE COMPANY are
being born.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:38.509
The motorcycle factory was created this year,
2017, with American investment.

00:10:38.509 --> 00:10:42.160
If you want to start a company in neighbouring
countries, you will need weeks or even months

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.369
to deal with all the paperwork.

00:10:43.369 --> 00:10:45.910
In Rwanda, you’re done with all that in
just 2 days.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:51.429
And, of course, this has attracted lots of
foreign investors, especially from China and

00:10:51.429 --> 00:10:52.429
America.

00:10:52.429 --> 00:10:53.769
And now you might wonder…

00:10:53.769 --> 00:10:54.769
How did they end up here?

00:10:54.769 --> 00:10:55.769
What’s Paul Kagame’s secret?

00:10:55.769 --> 00:11:02.649
Well… my dear friends here at VisualPolitik,
the answer has a light side and a dark side…

00:11:02.649 --> 00:11:05.410
TITLE: TOLERANCE AT GUNPOINT

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.480
Everyone believes it: Rwanda works.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:10.649
Streets are safe and tolerance between hutus
and tutsies is imposed by law.

00:11:10.649 --> 00:11:20.060
The Rwandan constitution itself forbids the
use of the words TUTSI and HUTU to refer to

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:21.170
a person.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:25.220
According to the government, all citizens
are Rwandans and no one should care about

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:26.350
their tribe of origin.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:30.850
Neither the media, nor institutions, are allowed
to say anything that could spark hatred or

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:32.679
open past scars.

00:11:32.679 --> 00:11:33.679
And…

00:11:33.679 --> 00:11:36.549
well… in fact they can’t even criticise
their government...

00:11:36.549 --> 00:11:40.980
Both the police and the military are present
all over the country to make sure everyone

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:42.220
follows these laws.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.329
Yes, it is true, Paul Kagame is a popular
president.

00:11:45.329 --> 00:11:49.209
Indeed, has his own YouTube channel and a
twitter and facebook account he uses almost

00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:50.309
daily.

00:11:50.309 --> 00:11:58.119
But no one else has the freedom to express
their ideas freely.

00:11:58.119 --> 00:11:59.420
And the same goes for the other political
parties.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:04.050
We are talking about a president who’s been
in power for 17 years and who wins elections

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:07.639
with outcomes bigger than 95% of the vote.

00:12:07.639 --> 00:12:12.379
As you can imagine, this is far from democratic.

00:12:12.379 --> 00:12:27.089
In other words, the Rwandan model is based
on three pillars: ease of investing and doing

00:12:27.089 --> 00:12:31.449
business, infrastructure development, and,
at the top, an authoritarian government that

00:12:31.449 --> 00:12:33.720
guarantees safety and tolerance…

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:36.259
at the expense of other human rights.

00:12:36.259 --> 00:12:40.769
And now is when we want to hear your opinion…

00:12:40.769 --> 00:12:45.269
Do you think this lack of democracy is legit
if the country can step out of poverty?

00:12:45.269 --> 00:12:49.389
Or… perhaps Rwanda would be better off if
they structured the country to a more democratic

00:12:49.389 --> 00:12:50.519
Western model?

00:12:50.519 --> 00:12:52.989
Please, leave your answer in the comment section
below.

